%N A162277 a(n) = A162276(n)/n.
%C A162277 a(n) is an odd integer >= 3, for all n.
%C A162277 a(n) is the least positive integer k such that A000120(n*k) != A000120(n), i.e., the index of the first row of A340351 that does not include n as a term. - _Pontus von Brömssen_, Nov 27 2026
%H A162277 Robert Israel, <a href="/A162277/b162277.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A162277 a(2^k-1) = 2^k+1. - _Robert Israel_, Sep 20 2018
%F A162277 From _Pontus von Brömssen_, Nov 27 2026: (Start)
%F A162277 a(2*n) = a(n).
%F A162277 a(n) = 3 if and only if n is not in A077459.
%F A162277 a(n) <= 2^(A000120(n)+1)-1. This follows from my comment in A000120 from Dec 13 2020. It appears that the stronger inequality a(n) <= 2^A000120(n)+1 holds, with equality if and only if n is in A023758.
%F A162277 (End)
